.TH LIBRJSS 3 "October 2026" "librjss 2.3.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
librjss \- async Rust client for Juragan Subsystem (JSS) / Frappe / ERPNext APIs.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SS Cargo dependency
.nf
\fB[dependencies]\fR
\fBlibrjss = { git = "https://github.com/mroczect/librjss.git", branch = "master" }\fR
.fi
.SS Import in Rust code
.nf
\fBuse librjss::{\fR
    \fBRjssClient, ClientConfig, AuthMode, JssError,\fR
    \fBSessionInfo, FrappeBoot, BootUser, BootUserInfo,\fR
    \fBSidebarPages, SidebarPage, NavbarSettings, NavbarItem,\fR
    \fBFrequentLink, PageInfo, ReportMeta, AppData,\fR
    \fBSysDefaults, UserInfo,\fR
\fB};\fR
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBlibrjss\fR is a lightweight asynchronous client that provides full access to a
JSS (Frappe / ERPNext) server. It supports:
.IP \[bu] 2
Cookie\-based session authentication and API\-key/secret token authentication.
.IP \[bu]
Automatic CSRF token and \fBfrappe.boot\fR extraction from the \fB/app\fR
dashboard, parsed through a JavaScript\-compatible reader (JSON5).
.IP \[bu]
Configurable retry with exponential backoff.
.IP \[bu]
Typed builders for reports and doctype CRUD, plus a full file upload/download API.
.IP \[bu]
A read\-only guard that refuses mutating requests unless the path is whitelisted.
.IP \[bu]
A rich error model mirroring Frappe JSON error responses.
.IP \[bu]
Unique trace ID per client for distributed tracing.
.PP
This manual documents every public module, struct, enum, trait, and method
available in librjss 2.3.0.
.SH CORE CONCEPTS
.SS RjssClient
Central struct holding configuration, HTTP client, session, credentials, boot
data, and the read\-only guard.
.PP
\fBConstructor:\fR
.RS 4
\fBRjssClient::new(config: ClientConfig) -> Result<Self, JssError>\fR
.br
Validates configuration, builds a reqwest client with a cookie jar, timeout,
and user\-agent, and installs the read\-only guard when enabled.
.RE
.PP
\fBAuthentication and session:\fR
.TP
\fBauthenticate(&mut self) -> Result<(), JssError>\fR
Logs in using session or token (depending on \fBAuthMode\fR). In session mode
it stores the credentials and calls login, which also fetches \fB/app\fR to
extract the CSRF token and \fBfrappe.boot\fR. In token mode it constructs a
synthetic \fBSessionInfo\fR and stores it.
.TP
\fBlogout(&mut self) -> Result<(), JssError>\fR
Only meaningful for \fBAuthMode::Session\fR. Sends a logout request with the
CSRF token, then clears both session and credentials.
.TP
\fBensure_session(&mut self) -> Result<(), JssError>\fR
Verifies the current session by calling \fBget_logged_user\fR. On 401, the
session is discarded and, if credentials are available, a fresh login is
performed automatically. Up to 3 attempts.
.PP
\fBAccessors:\fR
.TP
\fBsession_info(&self) -> Option<&SessionInfo>\fR
Current session data, if any.
.TP
\fBboot(&self) -> Option<&FrappeBoot>\fR
The boot data extracted from \fB/app\fR after login. Contains user info,
permissions, sidebar, versions, and more.
.TP
\fBbase_url(&self) -> &Url\fR
The base server URL.
.TP
\fBtrace_id(&self) -> &str\fR
UUID v4 for tracing/logging.
.TP
\fBis_readonly_guard_on(&self) -> bool\fR
Whether the read\-only guard is active.
.PP
\fBAuthenticated HTTP:\fR
.TP
\fBauthenticated_get(&self, path: &str) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
.TP
\fBauthenticated_post(&self, path: &str, body_json: &str) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
.TP
\fBauthenticated_put(&self, path: &str, body_json: &str) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
.TP
\fBauthenticated_delete(&self, path: &str) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
Send the corresponding HTTP request to the path joined with base_url. They
attach the appropriate authorization header (token or CSRF) and handle retry
with exponential backoff. Mutating methods (POST, PUT, DELETE) pass through
the read\-only guard first.
.TP
\fBpost_form(&self, path: &str, form: &[(&str, &str)]) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
Sends \fBapplication/x\-www\-form\-urlencoded\fR. Useful for APIs such as global
search, link search, and workflow transitions.
.PP
\fBPermission helpers (from boot data):\fR
.TP
\fBcan_read(&self, doctype: &str) -> bool\fR
.TP
\fBcan_write(&self, doctype: &str) -> bool\fR
.TP
\fBcan_create(&self, doctype: &str) -> bool\fR
.TP
\fBcan_submit(&self, doctype: &str) -> bool\fR
.TP
\fBcan_delete(&self, doctype: &str) -> bool\fR
.TP
\fBaccessible_doctypes(&self) -> Vec<String>\fR
Union of read, write, and create permissions, sorted.
.PP
\fBFile operations:\fR
.TP
\fBupload_file(&self, file_name: &str, file_content: Vec<u8>, doctype: &str, docname: &str, fieldname: &str) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
Uploads via multipart/form\-data to \fB/api/method/upload_file\fR. The
file name must not contain \fB/\fR, \fB\\\\\fR, or \fB..\fR.
.TP
\fBdownload_file(&self, file_url: &str) -> Result<Vec<u8>, JssError>\fR
Downloads a file from a relative URL (e.g.\fB"/files/photo.png"\fR). Returns
raw bytes. Absolute URLs and path traversal are rejected.
.TP
\fBdownload_file_to_path(&self, file_url: &str, save_path: &Path) -> Result<(), JssError>\fR
Same as above, but writes directly to disk.
.TP
\fBdownload_pdf_kartu_piutang(&self, doctype: &str, name: &str, format: &str, no_letterhead: bool) -> Result<Vec<u8>, JssError>\fR
Downloads a PDF for a specific print format via
\fB/api/method/frappe.utils.print_format.download_pdf\fR. Returns the raw
PDF bytes. Attaches CSRF and any token authorization.
.PP
\fBReports and resources:\fR
.TP
\fBreport(&self, name: &str) -> ReportBuilder\fR
Returns a builder for running a named Frappe query report.
.TP
\fBdoctype(&self, name: &str) -> ResourceBuilder\fR
Returns a builder for fetching document lists.
.TP
\fBget_doc(&self, doctype: &str, name: &str) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
Fetches a single document by name.
.TP
\fBget_doc_json(&self, doctype: &str, name: &str) -> Result<serde_json::Value, JssError>\fR
Shortcut returning a \fBserde_json::Value\fR.
.TP
\fBcreate_doc(&self, doctype: &str, data: &impl Serialize) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
.TP
\fBupdate_doc(&self, doctype: &str, name: &str, data: &impl Serialize) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
.TP
\fBdelete_doc(&self, doctype: &str, name: &str) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
.TP
\fBrun_report(&self, report_name: &str, filters: serde_json::Value) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
Runs a query report via \fBfrappe.desk.query_report.run\fR.
.TP
\fBcall_method(&self, method: &str, args: Option<HashMap<String, String>>) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
Calls a whitelisted server method with JSON POST body.
.PP
\fBFrappe\-specific convenience:\fR
.TP
\fBglobal_search(&self, query: &str, limit: u32, doctype: Option<&str>) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
Calls \fBfrappe.utils.global_search.search\fR.
.TP
\fBsearch_link(&self, txt: &str, doctype: &str, reference_doctype: &str, page_length: u32) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
Autocomplete for link fields: \fBfrappe.desk.search.search_link\fR.
.TP
\fBget_transitions(&self, doc_json: &str) -> Result<String, JssError>\fR
Raw workflow transitions: \fBfrappe.model.workflow.get_transitions\fR.
.TP
