.SS AuthMode
Authentication strategy selection.
.PP
.nf
\fBpub enum AuthMode {\fR
    \fBSession {\fR
        \fBemail: secrecy::SecretString,\fR
        \fBpassword: secrecy::SecretString,\fR
    \fB},\fR
    \fBToken {\fR
        \fBapi_key: String,\fR
        \fBapi_secret: secrecy::SecretString,\fR
    \fB},\fR
\fB}\fR
.fi
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBSession\fR \- logs in with email/password, manages session cookies, and
extracts the CSRF token and boot data from \fB/app\fR.
.IP \[bu]
\fBToken\fR \- sends \fBAuthorization: token api_key:api_secret\fR on every
request. No explicit login or logout is required. \fBlogout()\fR is a no-op
in this mode.
.SS ClientConfig
Configuration container validated at client creation.
.PP
.nf
\fBpub struct ClientConfig {\fR
    \fBpub base_url: reqwest::Url,\fR
    \fBpub auth_mode: AuthMode,\fR
    \fBpub expected_sitename: Option<String>,\fR
    \fBpub required_roles: Vec<String>,\fR
    \fBpub timeout_secs: u64,          // default 30\fR
    \fBpub max_retries: u32,           // default 3\fR
    \fBpub user_agent: String,\fR
    \fBpub insecure_ssl: bool,         // default false\fR
    \fBpub readonly_guard: bool,       // default true\fR
\fB}\fR
.fi
.PP
\fBMethods:\fR
.TP
\fBvalidate(&self) -> Result<(), JssError>\fR
Ensures HTTPS unless \fBinsecure_ssl\fR is true. For \fBSession\fR mode it
requires non\-empty email and password. Rejects dangerous URL schemes
(\fBdata\fR, \fBjavascript\fR, \fBvbscript\fR).
.TP
\fBfrom_env() -> Result<Self, JssError>\fR
Builds a config from environment variables (see \fBCONFIGURATION\fR).
.SS JssError
Comprehensive error type covering all failure modes.
.PP
.nf
\fBpub enum JssError {\fR
    \fBConfig(String),\fR
    \fBValidation(String),\fR
    \fBNetwork(reqwest::Error),\fR
    \fBHttp { status: StatusCode, body: String },\fR
    \fBApiError { exc_type: String, message: String, status: StatusCode },\fR
    \fBAuth(String),\fR
    \fBCsrf(String),\fR
    \fBPermission(String),\fR
    \fBSitenameMismatch { expected: String, actual: String },\fR
    \fBNotAuthenticated,\fR
    \fBRateLimited { retry_after: Option<u64> },\fR
    \fBParse(String),\fR
    \fBExpired,\fR
    \fBCancelled,\fR
    \fBFileOperation(String),\fR
    \fBInternal(String),\fR
\fB}\fR
.fi
.PP
\fBHelper methods:\fR
.TP
\fBfrom_api_response(status: StatusCode, body: &str) -> JssError\fR
Parses a Frappe JSON error body. If \fBexc_type\fR is present, returns
\fBApiError\fR; otherwise returns \fBHttp\fR.
.TP
\fBstatus_code(&self) -> StatusCode\fR
Maps each variant to an HTTP status code: \fBConfig\fR, \fBValidation\fR,
\fBInternal\fR, \fBParse\fR, \fBFileOperation\fR → 500; \fBNetwork\fR → 502;
\fBHttp\fR and \fBApiError\fR → carried status; \fBAuth\fR,
\fBNotAuthenticated\fR, \fBExpired\fR → 401; \fBCsrf\fR, \fBPermission\fR,
\fBSitenameMismatch\fR → 403; \fBRateLimited\fR → 429; \fBCancelled\fR → 503.
.SS SessionInfo
Session data stored after a successful login.
.PP
.nf
\fBpub struct SessionInfo {\fR
    \fBpub sid: secrecy::SecretString,\fR
    \fBpub csrf_token: secrecy::SecretString,\fR
    \fBpub full_name: Option<String>,\fR
    \fBpub sitename: String,\fR
    \fBpub roles: Vec<String>,\fR
\fB}\fR
.fi
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBsid\fR \- session ID from the login response (or "token\-mode" literal).
.IP \[bu]
\fBcsrf_token\fR \- token extracted from the \fB/app\fR page.
.IP \[bu]
\fBfull_name\fR \- user's full name (from boot or login response).
.IP \[bu]
\fBsitename\fR \- site name from \fBfrappe.boot\fR.
.IP \[bu]
\fBroles\fR \- user role list.
.SS FrappeBoot and related types
Data structure deserialized from the JavaScript \fBfrappe.boot\fR object on
the \fB/app\fR page. All fields have defaults (mostly \fBOption\fR or empty
collections), so missing keys never fail the whole deserialization.
.PP
