.SH READ-ONLY GUARD
By default, \fBlibrjss\fR installs a read\-only guard
(\fBreadonly_guard: true\fR). Any non\-idempotent request
(\fBPOST\fR, \fBPUT\fR, \fBDELETE\fR) whose path is not in the guard
whitelist is rejected with \fBJssError::Validation\fR before any network
I/O is performed.
.PP
Safe HTTP methods (\fBGET\fR, \fBHEAD\fR, \fBOPTIONS\fR) always pass.
.PP
Whitelisted POST paths include all read\-style Frappe endpoints, for example:
.RS 4
.nf
/api/method/login
/api/method/logout
/api/method/frappe.auth.get_logged_user
/api/method/frappe.client.get_count
/api/method/frappe.client.get_list
/api/method/frappe.client.get_value
/api/method/frappe.client.get
/api/method/frappe.client.validate_link
/api/method/frappe.desk.reportview.get_list
/api/method/frappe.desk.reportview.get_count
/api/method/frappe.desk.search.search_link
